    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d280">

                <pb facs="0363" n="265" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg265"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Goodnow.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-08-19"><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Two telegrams relative inquiry Nankin viceroys received. You will assure them
                    that announced policy of this Government rests on consideration for the Chinese
                    people not implicated in antiforeign <pb facs="0364" n="266" xml:id="pg266"/>
                    outrages, and will duly regard high personalities of Empress and Emperor. In
                    circular of July 3 to powers we said: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The policy of the United States is to seek a solution which may bring
                            about permanent peace and safety to China and to preserve Chinese
                            territorial and administrative entity.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>To this we adhere.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
